# OS Auditing Configuration file
# Enables PAM-based terminal (TTY) auditing for every user session, including
# root shells opened through sudo. Only sessions with a terminal produce TTY
# records, so daemon sessions such as cron add nothing.
# log_passwd is deliberately omitted, so input entered while terminal echo is
# disabled is not intentionally recorded.
session required pam_tty_audit.so enable=*
